  [atlas] answer A via openrouter:dots-studio/dots-3-note-preview:free (22.1s)  critic score: 10.0/10
     Canberra is the capital of Australia. It is not Sydney because the Australian Constitution required a separate federal territory; after a temporary seat in Melbourne, a site was chosen in 1908 and named Canberra, which became the permanent capital in 1927.
     sources: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra, https://www.britannica.com/place/Canberra, https://www.australia.gov.au/about-australia/our-country
